# Local settings for the web app. Copy to apps/web/.env.local (git-ignored); Next.js loads it for
# `next dev`, `next build` and `next start`. Everything here is read on the server and nothing
# reaches the browser: the app has no NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable and a page never calls a service.
# Placeholder values only; never a real secret (gitleaks runs in pre-commit and CI).

# Runtime environment: local | test | staging | prod. Unset means local; a value outside the set
# counts as prod, so a typo never opens a local-only page. The design catalogue (/design) exists
# only in local and test, and the internal shell shows this name.
CW_WEB_ENV=local

# The port is not set here: Next.js reads PORT from the process, and `make web-dev` and
# `make web-e2e` pass WEB_PORT from the root .env (3000 unless changed). A second working copy of
# the repository (docs/onboarding/local-dev.md, "Running a second clone") sets WEB_PORT=3200
# there and runs the services on 9201-9210. The app reads no service URL yet, so nothing in this
# file changes for that copy.
